% Repository-wide public boundary. Rust-first deterministic gate and thin shell/CI integration.

Purpose: prevent known private artifacts from entering the public Git tree or Docker
publication surface without reading private external data or echoing secret matches.

Inputs: complete Git index (or committed index in CI); explicit Docker-context file list.
Outputs: exit zero on allowed source, nonzero on violations; path/rule-only diagnostics.
Read staged blobs by object ID, not working-tree contents. Handle unusual filenames,
symlinks, unreadable/oversized blobs and subprocess errors by failing closed.

<vocabulary>
trusted: part of the immutable pinned image or an independently human-reviewed challenge specification.
untrusted: caller-provided source, compiled data, logs or metaprograms, never authority for the verdict.
invalid: bytes that fail UTF-8 decoding or a value failing the documented schema.
unsafe: a path that contains Docker mount delimiters or resolves through symlinks.
authorized: explicitly selected by the human in the invoking agent session.
complete: every record returned by git ls-files --stage -z; unmerged stages and read/limit errors fail the gate.
</vocabulary>
<contract_rules>
R-001 (MUST): inspect the complete selected index and actual staged blob content.
R-002 (MUST NOT): accept private runtime artifacts, credential files, known tokens,
private keys or personal absolute paths.
R-003 (MUST NOT): print matching secret contents, read external symlink targets,
upload data, mutate the index or publish anything.
R-004 (MUST): use synthetic negative tests, index/worktree disagreement tests, authored public-source positive tests, and an independent Docker-context/image canary test.
R-005 (MUST): document opt-in hooks, CI limitations and required human publication review.
R-006 (MUST NOT): equate a pattern scan with proof that arbitrary private information is absent.
</contract_rules>

The Rust implementation belongs to Rust/lean-agent/src/privacy.rs and
Rust/lean-agent/src/bin/claw-public-check.rs. Root .githooks/pre-commit and
.github/workflows/privacy.yml are thin integrations. Preserve existing policy work.
